hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1456","Narrated Abu Qatada:\n\nI heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying, \A good dream is from Allah"""
"1457","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, When the Day of Resurrection approaches ""1458"",t or.r- said"""
"1458","[AI-translation] Samit, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""The dream of a believer is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood.""
1459"""
"1459","Narrated Anas (رضي الله عنه): The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""The true good dream of a believer is one of the forty-six parts of prophecy."""
"1460","A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"""
"1461","I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying, Allah said"""
"1462","The hadith of Ibn Abbas: that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: ""I saw tonight in a dream a canopy dripping with butter and honey, and I see people scooping from it, some taking much and some taking little. And there was a rope extending from the earth to the heaven, and I saw you take hold of it and ascend. Then another man took hold of it and ascended. Then another man took hold of it and ascended. Then another man took hold of it and it broke, then it was rejoined for him."""" ""Abu Bakr said: """"O Messenger of Allah"", may my father be ransomed for you ""The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: """"You got some right and erred in some."""" He said: """"By Allah"""
"1463","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""I was shown in a dream that I was brushing my teeth with a siwak. Then two men came to me, one of them older than the other. I handed the siwak to the younger of the two, but it was said to me, 'Give it to the older one.' So I handed it to the older of the two.""
1464"""
"1464","Narrated Abu Musa: The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""I saw in a dream that I was migrating from Mecca to a land in which there were date palms. My thoughts went to the possibility that it was Al-Yamama or Hajr, but it turned out to be Al-Madinah, i.e., Yathrib. In this dream of mine, I also saw that I brandished a sword, and it broke in the middle, and behold, that symbolized the casualties which the believers suffered on the Day of (the battle of) Uhud. Then I brandished the sword again, and it became better than it was before, and behold, that symbolized the victory which Allah brought about, and the gathering of the believers. I also saw cows, and by Allah, that was good, and they symbolized the believers on the Day of Uhud, and (the fact that they were good indicated) the good which Allah brought about, and the reward of true faith which Allah gave us after the Day of Badr."""
"1465","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: Musailamah al-Kadhdhab (the liar) came during the lifetime of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and began to say: ""If Muhammad appoints me as his successor, I will follow him."" He came to Madinah with a great number of his people. Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) went out to him accompanied by Thabit bin Qais bin Shammas, and in the hand of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) was a piece of a palm branch. He stopped before Musailamah, who was among his companions, and said: ""If you were to ask me for this piece (of palm branch), I would not give it to you. You cannot escape the command of Allah concerning you. If you turn away, Allah will surely destroy you. Indeed, I see in you that which was shown to me in a vision, and this is Thabit who will answer you on my behalf."" Then he turned away from him.

Ibn 'Abbas said: I asked about the saying of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ): ""You are the one about whom I was shown what I was shown,"" (and was told its meaning)."
"1466","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, The sign of Belief is to love the Ansar"""
"1467","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) very often used to ask his companions, Did anyone of you see a dream?"" So dreams would be narrated to him by those whom Allah wished to tell. One morning the Prophet (ﷺ) said"""
